IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-post2016`

-- Tests for Part 8, Chapter 3 (regulations 29 to 39, lines 353 to 517). Expected values are written from the text.
-- A week is named by its first day.

§ `Part 8, Chapter 3`

§§ `Regulation 39: the time limit`

GIVEN received IS A DATE
      further IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `An application for a credit`
`an application received` received further MEANS
    `An application for a credit` WITH
        `the date the application is received` IS received
        `the person who decides considers it reasonable to allow further time in the circumstances` IS further

-- Regulation 34(1)(b), 36, 37: before the end of the year following that in which the week falls. The week of 5 June 2026 falls
-- in the year 6 April 2026 to 5 April 2027; the year following ends on 5 April 2028 (fork F24: that day counts).
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 5 4 2028) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 34(1)(b)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) FALSE))
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 36` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) TRUE)
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 37` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 5 4 2028) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 37` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 1 1 2040) FALSE))
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 37` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 1 1 2040) TRUE)
-- Received before the week: before the end of the year following it.
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 36` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE)
-- A week of 5 April 2026 begins in the year before: the year following it ends on 5 April 2027.
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 36` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 4 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 5 4 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 36` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 4 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2027) FALSE))
-- Regulation 35: after the end of the year in which the week falls (5 April 2027), with no upper bound.
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 35` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 5 4 2027) FALSE))
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 35` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT `the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 35` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 1 1 2060) FALSE)
-- Further time is only for (a): it does not make an early regulation 35 application in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is received in time` `an application under regulation 35` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) `and the application being` (`an application received` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 29: credits under the 1975 Regulations`

#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 7A (credits for carer's allowance or carer support payment)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 8A (credits for unemployment)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces)` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `some other provision of the 1975 Regulations` `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- Regulation 24(2): not for a week beginning before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)` `for the week beginning` (Date 3 4 2016))
#ASSERT `a credit under the 1975 Regulations also counts for the 2014 Act` `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)` `for the week beginning` (Date 6 4 2016)

§§ `Regulation 30: working tax credit`

-- A person not in a couple, to whom working tax credit is paid for the week.
GIVEN paid IS A BOOLEAN
      employed IS A BOOLEAN
      selfemp IS A BOOLEAN
      excepted IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid`
`a person on tax credit` paid employed selfemp excepted other election MEANS
    `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid` WITH
        `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS paid
        `the person is an employed earner in the week` IS employed
        `the person is a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution` IS selfemp
        `the person is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS excepted
        `the working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
        `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
        `the person is the member assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
        `the earnings of each member of the couple are assessed` IS FALSE
        `the working tax credit is paid to the person` IS TRUE
        `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS other
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS election
        `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS 123

-- (1)(a) an employed earner; (b) a small-profits self-employed earner; (c) excepted by regulation 43. Credited with earnings equal to
-- the lower earnings limit in force for the week (here 123).
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `the earnings credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the earnings credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS 0
-- Working tax credit must be paid in respect of the week.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (3)(a): not for a week in which the person is entitled to credits under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (3)(b): not for a woman whose reduced rate election is in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- Regulation 24(2): not for a week beginning before 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a person on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 3 4 2016))

-- (2): where working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple.
GIVEN onlyone IS A BOOLEAN
      assessed IS A BOOLEAN
      each IS A BOOLEAN
      paidto IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid`
`a couple on tax credit` onlyone assessed each paidto MEANS
    `Facts for credit while working tax credit is paid` WITH
        `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
        `the person is an employed earner in the week` IS TRUE
        `the person is a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold, who would otherwise be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution` IS FALSE
        `the person is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS FALSE
        `the working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS TRUE
        `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS onlyone
        `the person is the member assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS assessed
        `the earnings of each member of the couple are assessed` IS each
        `the working tax credit is paid to the person` IS paidto
        `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS FALSE
        `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS 123
-- (2)(a): only one member's earnings assessed: that member, whoever the credit is paid to.
#ASSERT `the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` (`a couple on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` (`a couple on tax credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- (2)(b): both members' earnings assessed: the member to whom it is paid.
#ASSERT `the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` (`a couple on tax credit` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` (`a couple on tax credit` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- Neither (a) nor (b) applies to a couple where nobody's earnings are assessed.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is the person in respect of whom working tax credit is paid` (`a couple on tax credit` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a couple on tax credit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 30` (`a couple on tax credit` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))

§§ `Regulation 31: universal credit`

#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 31` (Date 5 6 2026) `given` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 31` (Date 5 6 2026) `given` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 31` (Date 29 3 2016) `given` TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 32: men approaching pensionable age`

GIVEN man IS A BOOLEAN
      born IS A DATE
      woman IS A DATE
      week IS A DATE
      absent IS A NUMBER
      selfemp IS A BOOLEAN
      small IS A BOOLEAN
      excepted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age`
`a man` man born woman week absent selfemp small excepted MEANS
    `Facts for a man approaching pensionable age` WITH
        `the person is a man` IS man
        `the man's date of birth` IS born
        `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS woman
        `the first day of the week` IS week
        `the number of days in the year of the week that the man was absent from Great Britain` IS absent
        `the man is a self-employed earner` IS selfemp
        `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for profits below the small profits threshold` IS small
        `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001` IS excepted
        `the lower earnings limit in force for the week` IS 123

-- A man born 15 May 1953, who attains the pensionable age of a woman born that day on 15 November 2015 (the year beginning
-- 6 April 2015) and 65 on 15 May 2018 (the year beginning 6 April 2018).
-- (2)(a), (b): the years 2015, 2016 and 2017 - but a Chapter 3 credit needs a week beginning on or after 6 April 2016 (regulation 24(2)).
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 5 4 2018) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 6 4 2018) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2015) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (2)(a): the first year is the one in which he attains the age. If that is the year beginning 6 April 2017 (a woman born the same
-- day reaching pensionable age on 1 January 2018), a week in the year before it is out and a week in it is in.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 1 1 2018) (Date 20 6 2017) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Credited with earnings equal to the lower earnings limit.
#ASSERT `the earnings credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 123
#ASSERT `the earnings credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2018) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- (1): a man born before 6 October 1953.
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 5 10 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 6 10 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` FALSE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (3): not a year in which he is absent from Great Britain for more than 182 days.
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 182 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 183 FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (4): a self-employed man only if he would be treated as having paid a Class 2 contribution but for small profits, or is excepted.
#ASSERT NOT (`earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `earnings are credited under regulation 32` (`a man` TRUE (Date 15 5 1953) (Date 15 11 2015) (Date 20 6 2016) 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 33: forces spouses, from 6 April 2016`

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      qef IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A BOOLEAN
      received IS A MAYBE DATE
      form IS A BOOLEAN
      info IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
`a forces spouse` first qef other election received form info MEANS
    `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces` WITH
        `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS TRUE
        `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
        `the first day of the week` IS first
        `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS qef
        `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS other
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS election
        `the date the Secretary of State receives the application` IS received
        `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances` IS form
        `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS info

#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE)
-- (3): a year beginning on or after 6 April 2016.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 4 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 5 4 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
-- (3), (4), (5), (6): as for regulation 28.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 12 6 2020)) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 13 6 2020)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 33` (`a forces spouse` (Date 6 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2020)) TRUE FALSE))

§§ `Regulation 34: child benefit`

GIVEN week IS A DATE
      awarded IS A BOOLEAN
      partner IS A BOOLEAN
      resides IS A BOOLEAN
      shares IS A BOOLEAN
      ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      free IS A BOOLEAN
      app IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
      efs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit in respect of child benefit`
`a child benefit case` week awarded partner resides shares ordinary free app efs MEANS
    `Facts for credit in respect of child benefit` WITH
        `the first day of the week` IS week
        `child benefit is awarded to the person for any part of the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS awarded
        `the person is the partner of a person to whom child benefit is awarded for the week` IS partner
        `the partner resides with the person to whom child benefit is awarded` IS resides
        `the partner shares responsibility for the child with that person` IS shares
        `the partner is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS ordinary
        `the partner is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS free
        `the partner has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS app
        `the earnings factors of the person to whom child benefit is awarded for the year exceed the qualifying earnings factor` IS efs

-- (1)(a): awarded child benefit for any part of the week in respect of a child under 12. No application is needed.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE))
-- Regulation 24(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 3 4 2016) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE))
-- (1)(b), (2), (3): the partner of the person awarded child benefit.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE)
-- Each of (2)(a) to (e) and (3) is needed.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)) FALSE))
-- (2)(e): the application in accordance with regulation 39: too late, or too late with further time allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) FALSE)) TRUE))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 34` (`a child benefit case` (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) TRUE)) TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 35: care for a child under 12`

GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship to the child cared for`
      app IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
      more IS A BOOLEAN
      elected IS A BOOLEAN
      `this one` IS A BOOLEAN
      requested IS A BOOLEAN
      declared IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12`
`a carer` relationship app more elected `this one` requested declared MEANS
    `Facts for credit for caring for a child under 12` WITH
        `the person provided care in the week in respect of a child under the age of 12` IS TRUE
        `the person's relationship to the child` IS relationship
        `the person was ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS TRUE
        `child benefit was awarded to another person in respect of the child, or each child, and the week` IS TRUE
        `that other person's earnings factors, other than those derived from a regulation 34 credit, exceed the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS TRUE
        `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS app
        `the application includes the name and date of birth of each child cared for` IS TRUE
        `the Secretary of State or the Commissioners requested a declaration by the other person` IS requested
        `the application includes a declaration by the other person that the conditions in regulation 35(2) are satisfied` IS declared
        `the application specifies the week or weeks in which each child was cared for` IS TRUE
        `more than one person could be credited for the week` IS more
        `those persons have elected, with the agreement of the other person, which of them is to be credited` IS elected
        `this person is the one elected` IS `this one`

`given` MEANS `the credit is given`
`not given` MEANS `the credit is not given`
`discretion` MEANS `the credit is left to the Secretary of State's discretion`
`late enough` MEANS JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE)

-- (1) to (3): a grandparent who provided care, ordinarily resident, child benefit awarded to B whose earnings factors exceed, and an
-- application after the end of the year in which the week (5 June 2026) falls (5 April 2027).
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `given`
-- (3)(c): the application is needed, and under regulation 39(b) it is after the end of the year in which the week falls.
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` (JUST (`an application received` (Date 5 4 2027) FALSE)) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`
-- (2)(b): a person specified in paragraph (6).
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `none of the relationships in regulation 35(6)` `late enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`
-- Regulation 24(2).
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 3 4 2016) EQUALS `not given`
-- (5)(b): where a declaration by B was requested, it must be included.
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `given`
-- (4): more than one person could be credited: the elected person is credited and no other; in default of agreement, the Secretary
-- of State decides.
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `given`
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `discretion`
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `a grandparent` `late enough` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `discretion`
-- The discretion arises only if the other conditions are met.
#ASSERT `whether a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 35` (`a carer` `none of the relationships in regulation 35(6)` `late enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026) EQUALS `not given`

-- (6): the persons specified.
#ASSERT `the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `a non-resident parent`
#ASSERT `the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `a great-great-grandparent`
#ASSERT `the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `a son or daughter of a person in regulation 35(6)(e) to (i)`
#ASSERT `the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `a spouse, former spouse, civil partner, former civil partner, partner or former partner of a parent's sibling whose son or daughter the child is`
#ASSERT NOT (`the relationship is one regulation 35(6) specifies` `none of the relationships in regulation 35(6)`)
-- (7): a sibling includes a sibling of the half blood, a step sibling and an adopted sibling.
#ASSERT `the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` TRUE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` FALSE `or` TRUE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` TRUE `or` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as a sibling under regulation 35(7)` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE `or` FALSE)
-- (8): a partner is the other member of a couple not married or civil partners but living together as if they were.
#ASSERT `the person counts as a partner under regulation 35(8)` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as a partner under regulation 35(8)` TRUE `and` TRUE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as a partner under regulation 35(8)` TRUE `and` FALSE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person counts as a partner under regulation 35(8)` FALSE `and` FALSE `and` TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 36: foster parents`

GIVEN approval IS A `Approval as a foster parent`
      ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      free IS A BOOLEAN
      app IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
GIVETH A `Facts for credit as a foster parent`
`a foster parent` approval ordinary free app MEANS
    `Facts for credit as a foster parent` WITH
        `the person's approval` IS approval
        `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain` IS ordinary
        `the person is not undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody` IS free
        `the person has applied to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS app

`in time` MEANS JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)
`england` MEANS `a foster parent approved under Part 5 of the Fostering Services (England) Regulations 2011`

-- (1), (2): approved under one of the four regimes, ordinarily resident in Great Britain and not in custody, and applying to HMRC.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `a kinship carer approved under Part 5 of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `a foster carer approved under Part 7 of the Looked After Children (Scotland) Regulations 2009` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `a foster parent approved under Part 2 of the Foster Placement (Children) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1996` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `not approved under any of those provisions` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` FALSE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE FALSE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (3): an application received by HMRC in accordance with regulation 39.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE TRUE NOTHING) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) FALSE))) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE TRUE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) TRUE))) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- Regulation 24(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 36` (`a foster parent` `england` TRUE TRUE `in time`) `for the week beginning` (Date 3 4 2016))

§§ `Regulation 37: caring`

GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
      benefits IS A LIST OF `Relevant benefit`
      considers IS A BOOLEAN
      `schedule 1B` IS A BOOLEAN
      ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      custody IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A BOOLEAN
      app IS A MAYBE `An application for a credit`
      `declaration of hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefit stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      requested IS A BOOLEAN
      signed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for credit for caring`
`a carer for` hours benefits considers `schedule 1B` ordinary custody election app `declaration of hours` `names` `benefit stated` requested signed MEANS
    `Facts for credit for caring` WITH
        `the hours the person cared for another person or persons in the week` IS hours
        `the benefit each person cared for is entitled to for the week` IS benefits
        `the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate` IS considers
        `paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B to the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987 applies to the person` IS `schedule 1B`
        `the person is ordinarily resident in Great Britain in the week` IS ordinary
        `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` IS custody
        `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week` IS election
        `the person has applied to the Secretary of State` IS app
        `the application includes a declaration by the applicant that the applicant cares for 20 or more hours in a week` IS `declaration of hours`
        `the application includes the name and, where known, the national insurance number of each person cared for` IS `names`
        `the application says, where applicable, which relevant benefit each person cared for is entitled to` IS `benefit stated`
        `the Secretary of State requested a declaration by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS requested
        `the application includes a declaration signed by an appropriate person as to the level of care` IS signed

`attendance` MEANS LIST `attendance allowance`
`good application` MEANS JUST (`an application received` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE)

-- (2)(a)(i): 20 or more hours caring for a person entitled to a relevant benefit; (5), (6), 39: an application.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 19 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- Each of the persons cared for must be entitled to a relevant benefit.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 (LIST `attendance allowance`, `none of those benefits`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 (LIST `attendance allowance`, `armed forces independence payment`) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- (2)(a)(ii): or the Secretary of State considers that level of care appropriate.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 (LIST `none of those benefits`) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 25 EMPTY TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- Nobody cared for, no benefit and no judgment: not engaged in caring.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 25 EMPTY FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (3): not engaged in caring while not ordinarily resident in Great Britain, or in custody.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (5): without an application, no credit under (2)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (6): the application must include (a), (b), (c) and, where requested, (d).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- Regulation 39: the application in time (kind regulation 37): too late without further time.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) FALSE)) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST (`an application received` (Date 6 4 2028) TRUE)) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- (2)(b): paragraph 4, 5 or 6 of Schedule 1B applies: no application needed and no hours.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 0 EMPTY FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 0 EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026))
-- (8), read literally (fork F25): a woman with an election in force needs no application, so she is credited under (2)(a) without one.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 5 6 2026)
-- Regulation 24(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 37` (`a carer for` 20 `attendance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `good application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `for the week beginning` (Date 3 4 2016))
-- (4): relevant benefits are the listed ones, not "none".
#ASSERT `the benefit is a relevant benefit` `attendance allowance`
#ASSERT `the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate`
#ASSERT NOT (`the benefit is a relevant benefit` `none of those benefits`)
-- (7): an appropriate person is involved in the health or social care of the person cared for and considered appropriate by the Secretary of State.
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an appropriate person` FALSE `and` TRUE)

§§ `Regulation 38: an additional period`

GIVEN circumstance IS A `Circumstance of an additional period of credit`
      day IS A DATE
      week IS A DATE
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for an additional period of credit`
`an additional period` circumstance day week entitled MEANS
    `Facts for an additional period of credit` WITH
        `the circumstance` IS circumstance
        `the day entitlement begins, or the first day of the week in which it ends` IS day
        `the first day of the week` IS week
        `the person is entitled in the week under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations to be credited because of carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support` IS entitled

`before` MEANS `before becoming entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
`after ceasing` MEANS `after ceasing to be entitled to carer's allowance or the carer support payment component of carer support`
`after 37 ceases` MEANS `after a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied`

-- (1)(a): twelve weeks before the day entitlement begins (Thursday 1 October 2026). The 84 days before it are 9 July to 30 September; the
-- weeks begin on Thursdays, so the twelve are those beginning 9 July to 24 September.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 9 7 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 24 9 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 2 7 2026) FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 1 10 2026) FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 10 2026) (Date 8 10 2026) FALSE))
-- (1)(b): twelve weeks following the end of the week in which entitlement ends (that week began on 5 June 2026): weeks beginning
-- 12 June to 28 August.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after ceasing` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 12 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after ceasing` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 28 8 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after ceasing` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 5 6 2026) FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after ceasing` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 4 9 2026) FALSE))
-- (2): not in a week in which the person is entitled to credits under regulation 7A of the 1975 Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after ceasing` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 19 6 2026) TRUE))
-- (1)(c): the same twelve weeks after a week in which regulation 37(2)(a) ceases to be satisfied; (2) does not touch it.
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after 37 ceases` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 12 6 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after 37 ceases` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 28 8 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT `a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after 37 ceases` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 19 6 2026) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `after 37 ceases` (Date 5 6 2026) (Date 4 9 2026) FALSE))
-- Regulation 24(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 38` (`an additional period` `before` (Date 1 4 2016) (Date 3 4 2016) FALSE))
